    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Bangia</b></i> is an extant genus of division Rhodophyta that grows in marine or freshwater habitats. <i>Bangia</i> has small thalli with rapid growth and high reproductive output, and exhibits behavior characteristic of r-selected species. The plants are attached by down-growing rhizoids, usually in dense purple-black to rust-colored clumps. The chloroplasts of <i>Bangia</i>, like others in the division Rhodophyta, contain chlorophyll a and sometimes chlorophyll d, as well as accessory pigments such as phycobilin pigments and xanthophylls. Depending...",
